{"FixedQueuePool.shutdown() sets worker.shutdown = True, which can cause workers to exit their main loop after finishing at most one in-flight item, leaving additional queued items unprocessed despite calling q.shutdown(immediate=False)": 0.8151499032974243, "ResultsStrategyFactory.shutdown() shuts down and nulls queue_pool independent of the returned strategy lifecycle, so callers/tests that only shut down the factory can leave the strategy's daemon commit thread running against a shut down pool": 0.8612368702888489, "FixedQueuePool creates work queues via queue.Queue() without a maxsize, so they grow without limit. Since SimpleQueueProcessingStrategy.submit() never blocks or raises MessageRejected, the Arroyo stream processor has no backpressure signal and will keep fetching from Kafka unboundedly, risking OOM if workers fall behind": 0.9259861707687378, "In SimpleQueueProcessingStrategy.close(), the commit thread is stopped before queue_pool.shutdown() drains the worker queues. Offsets completed by workers during the drain window are never committed, causing unnecessary message reprocessing on consumer restart": 0.9368733763694763, "The OffsetTracker uses a contiguous range loop to find committable offsets. Kafka offsets can have gaps (e.g. from log compaction or transactions), which will cause the loop to break early and permanently stall offset commits for that partition": 0.7349881529808044}